In C, modulo operator % cannot be used on float variables (causes compiler error: invalid operands to binary expression float and int).
Convert temperature to integer tenths and format with sprintf:
int t_tenths = (int)(temp_c * 10.0f);
int t_int = t_tenths / 10;
int t_frac = t_tenths % 10;
if (t_frac < 0) t_frac = -t_frac;
char lcd_buf[17];
sprintf(lcd_buf, "TEMP: %d.%d C [OK]", t_int, t_frac);
LCD_Set_Cursor(2, 1);
LCD_String(lcd_buf);
